{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>At the morning watch.</b> The three divisions of the night are called אַשְׁמוּרָה, and the one before morning he calls אַשְׁמֹרֶת הַבֹּקֶר. And I say: since the night is divided into watches for the song of the ministering angels, shift after shift, into three divisions, therefore it is called אַשְׁמֹרֶת — and this is what Onkelos translates 'מַטְּרַת'." "<b>And He looked.</b> And He gazed — that is, He turned toward them to destroy them. And its Targum 'וְאִסְתְּכִי' is likewise a term of gazing, as in 'שְׂדֵה צוֹפִים' (Numbers 23) — חֲקַל סָכוּתָא." "<b>In a pillar of fire and cloud.</b> A pillar of cloud descends and makes it like mud, and a pillar of fire boils it, and the hooves of their horses slip (Mekhilta)." "<b>And He threw.</b> A term of confusion — אשדורד\"י שון בְּלַעַ\"ז. He threw them into confusion; He removed their leadership. And we learned in the chapters of Rabbi Eliezer son of Rabbi Yosi HaGelili: Every place where מְהוּמָה is stated, it is a thundering of sound, and this is the father of them all: ״וַיַּרְעֵם יהוה בְּקוֹל גָּדוֹל וְגוֹ׳ עַל פְּלִשְׁתִּים וַיְהֻמֵּם״ (I Samuel 7)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {3 "The la'az אשדורד\"י appears corrupt or idiosyncratic; transliterated as written."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:26.902791121Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}